course: dictionary
lesson: 5868
title: Words that come from a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person comes from. Mancunian is one of them. A Mancunian is a person who comes from or lives in Manchester, a big city in north-west England. The word can also describe things, so it can be an adjective: a Mancunian accent is an accent from Manchester.
explain: Look at the ending. Many words that link a person to a place end in -ian, like Italian for someone from Italy. When you meet a word like this, ask: what place is it about? Then check your idea in the sentence.
explain: Read the context. Kai's cousin says, «You're 10, our kid», and then, «shops shouldn't even sell you that». The clue is in Manchester: our kid is a Mancunian way of saying brother or close family member. Swap in your meaning. If «our kid» means brother and the sentence still makes sense, you are right.
fact: Mancunian means a person from Manchester, or something to do with Manchester.
fact: Mancunian can be a noun (a Mancunian, Mancunians) or an adjective (Mancunian).
fact: Manchester is a big city in north-west England, known for football, music and a strong local accent.
fact: «Our kid» is Mancunian for a brother or close family member.
fact: Many words ending in -ian link a person to a place, like Italian or Mancunian.
exercise: What is a Mancunian? | A kind of football boot | A person who lives in London | *A person who comes from or lives in Manchester | A type of music
exercise: In «You're 10, our kid», what does «our kid» mean in Mancunian speech? | A shop | *A brother or close family member | A football team | A ten-year-old child
exercise: Which phrase uses Mancunian as an adjective? | The Mancunians cheered | Kai is a Mancunian | Two Mancunians walked in | *a Mancunian accent
test: Kai's cousin says «You're 10, our kid». What does «our kid» mean? | A shop | A ten-year-old child | *A close family member, like a brother | A football
test: In «a proud Mancunian», what kind of word is Mancunian? | *Noun | Adjective | Adverb | Verb
exam: Which word means a person from Manchester? | Scouser | Glaswegian | *Mancunian | Londoner
